join detective right
detective: [NIECE], I know why Dracula collapsed.
join niece left
niece (disappointed): What's that, dear?
detective: Your plot to swap out Dracula's will required you to get your hands on his safe key.
detective: The one he keeps on his person at all times.
detective (thinking): You needed a way to get him vulnerable.
detective (speaking): Of course, a dose of garlic was the perfect way to do that.
detective (thinking): But there's just one problem. You're a vampire too. You can't be the one working with the garlic.
detective: You also don't have easy access to the food Dracula eats.
detective (speaking): All that said, the human cook was the perfect accomplice.
detective: You bribed [COOK] to poison Dracula and knock him out for just enough time for you to snatch the key, swap the will, and return the key like nothing ever happened.
detective: But things didn't exactly go as planned did they?
niece (speaking): Well then, dear. I suppose I don't need to say anything.
niece: Figuring out my plan, it makes you almost as brilliant as I am for coming up with it.
niece (disappointed): It still doesn't tell you who killed uncle, though.
join detective_thinking right
detective_thinking: She's right. I'm still not certian who stabbed Dracula, but I feel like I'm close.
detective_thinking: Who would have been in Dracula's room around the time he was waking up from the garlic?
detective_thinking: If I combine [NIECE] and [COOK]'s secret' with an answer to that question, I think I'll have solved it.
